{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And you shall count for yourselves from the morrow of the Shabbat.</b> Through these seven weeks between the two appointed seasons — the barley harvest and the wheat harvest — the laws of Shemittah apply to them, and they are what Jeremiah referred to: שבועות חוקות קציר ישמור לנו, and Rashi explained: the seven weeks that He established for us in them two harvest laws — the law of the Omer and the Two Loaves — He will keep for us, that the harvest shall be in its season. Therefore a great matter depends on their counting, so as to serve as a model and a remembrance: just as we count days and weeks, and after the seventh Shabbat we sanctify the fiftieth day, so must we do with Shemittah and Yovel. And the entirety of the rebukes in this book were said only concerning the canceling of Shemittot, for they contain forty-nine types of punishment, corresponding to the forty-nine years of the Yovel cycle, if one cancels Shemittot during them." "<b>From the morrow of the Shabbat.</b> If you say it means the morrow of the Shabbat of Creation, sometimes you count fifty, and sometimes fifty-two, and sometimes fifty-four, and sometimes fifty-six — neither less nor more. And a mnemonic: לא בד״ו פסח — Pesach never falls on ב, ד, or ו (i.e., Sunday, Wednesday, or Friday). If so, how do I fulfill ממחרת השבת? From the morrow of the Festival day (Yom Tov)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {0 "The comment cites and explicates Rashi on Jeremiah 5:24; the compiler's voice integrates it without naming Rashi in the main flow, but the text explicitly writes ופרש״י 'and Rashi explained,' which is rendered directly."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:14:36.847684284Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}